+## The local CI suite (the GH gates, for free)
+
+The GitHub Actions gates in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` can be run locally
+without burning runner minutes — the ubuntu leg in a Linux container, the
+macOS leg natively. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` itself is untouched; this is a
+local replica, gate-for-gate:
+
+```bash
+tools/ci-local.sh               # all 8 gates in the container (the ubuntu leg)
+tools/ci-local.sh --fast        # gates 1-2 only: lint + unit tests (~10s loop)
+tools/ci-local.sh --mac         # the same 8 gates natively on macOS
+tools/ci-local.sh --native      # alias for --mac
+tools/ci-local.sh --windows-cross  # EXPERIMENTAL: compile-only windows build
+```
+
+The container is `Dockerfile.ci` (ubuntu 24.04, matching `ubuntu-latest`):
+it installs the pinned Odin release tarball exactly like the workflow's
+`Install Odin` step (linux/arm64 + amd64), the workflow's X11 link deps, and
+bakes the rlsw software-raylib shadow so warm runs skip the ~40s clone+build.
+`tools/ci-local.sh` builds the image (layer-cached), then runs the suite with
+the same order and stop-on-fail semantics as CI.
+
+**Gate mapping (GH CI step ↔ local stage):**
+
+| GH CI step | Local stage |
+|---|---|
+| Purity + grep gates (ODN-1) | `tools/lint.sh` |
+| Core unit tests (determinism + topology) | `odin test core` |
+| Game builds (app.bin compiles + links) | `odin build app -out:app.bin` |
+| Golden harness (T1 + T2 + replay gate) | `tools/harness.sh run` |
+| W1 drift-rejection negative test | `tools/harness.sh drift-check` |
+| Assist preview cross-check (R2a preview == sim) | `tools/harness.sh preview-check` |
+| PP_DEBUG overlay builds (compile gate) | `odin build app -define:PP_DEBUG=true` + `odin build harness -define:PP_DEBUG=true` |
+| Stats stream replay-identity | `tools/harness.sh stats-check pause` + `qos_contention` |
+| Upload diff bundles on failure | `goldens/_reports/` (bind-mounted out of the container) |
+
+**Artifact isolation (deliberate design):** the container never sees host
+build products — the image COPYs the tracked tree (`.dockerignore` strips
+`bin/`, `tools/raylib-sw/`, `goldens/_reports/`, `app*.bin`, …), so linux
+artifacts live and die inside the container. The only writable host surface
+is `goldens/_reports/`, so failure diff bundles surface on the host. The
+native leg builds into the worktree normally. The two legs share no artifact
+state — a run on either platform can never be poisoned by the other.
+
+**Known traps:**
+
+- The native leg warns loudly when your local `odin version` doesn't match
+  `.odin-version` — the goldens can drift on a toolchain difference; CI uses
+  the pinned release tarball. A same-month nightly prints an informational
+  note instead (verified bit-identical goldens vs the release tarball). The
+  container leg always uses the pin.
+- Goldens must be bit-identical in the container (software rendering is
+  platform-independent by design). A hash difference in-container is a REAL
+  finding — report it, don't paper over it.
+- Architecture: GH's `ubuntu-latest` is x86_64; on Apple Silicon the default
+  local container is linux/arm64. The T2 goldens are arch-independent by
+  design (`-ffp-contract=off` in `build_raylib_sw.sh`), but to replicate the
+  x64 runner leg exactly: `docker build --platform linux/amd64` +
+  `docker run --platform linux/amd64` (emulated; slower).
+- `--fast` is only fast WARM: the first fast run pays the full image build
+  (apt + odin fetch + raylib bake), and any `tools/` change invalidates the
+  bake layer.
+- No per-gate timeouts (macOS ships no GNU `timeout`): a hung gate blocks
+  the loop — Ctrl-C and fix the cause. GH CI bounds runs with its job
+  timeout; the local replica keeps parity by staying simple.
+- Docker not running? The script says so plainly — it's a dev tool, not CI.
+- `--windows-cross` is experimental and probes the LOCAL toolchain by
+  default: the pinned Odin release cannot cross-link to Windows from macOS
+  or Linux ("Linking for cross compilation for this platform is not yet
+  supported"), and `vendor:raylib/windows/` ships no prebuilt lib — the gate
+  reports the failure and exits 0-with-warning.
+
