+---
+title: 'Local CI suite (container replica of the GH CI gates)'
+type: 'feature'
+created: '2026-08-16'
+status: 'in-review'
+baseline_commit: 'e7fa548'
+review_loop_iteration: 0
+context: []
+---
+
+<frozen-after-approval reason="human-owned intent (user ruling 2026-08-16) — do not modify unless human renegotiates">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** GitHub Actions is billing-blocked (spending limit since 2026-08-16); the repo's CI gates (`tools/lint.sh`, `odin test core`, the app build, the golden harness, drift/preview checks, PP_DEBUG builds, stats checks) can no longer run for free on GH. The workflow `.github/workflows/ci.yml` must stay byte-identical.
+
+**Approach:** Add a LOCAL replica of the GH CI gates: `Dockerfile.ci` reproduces the ubuntu leg (pinned Odin tarball for linux/arm64+amd64, X11 link deps); `tools/ci-local.sh` is the one entrypoint — all 8 gates in the container by default, `--fast` = gates 1–2, `--mac`/`--native` = the same gates natively on macOS (loud warning on odin pin mismatch), `--windows-cross` = experimental compile-only gate (report + exit 0-with-warning if the toolchain fights). README section documents it.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- The workflow is the spec: ALL 8 run steps (lint → odin test core → app.bin build → harness run → drift-check → preview-check → PP_DEBUG builds → stats-check pause + qos_contention), same order, stop-on-fail. (The briefing listed 7; `tools/harness.sh drift-check` was omitted — the workflow wins.)
+- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` byte-identical to base — prove zero diff in the PR.
+- No gameplay/core/harness logic changes; a real gate failure at base is REPORTED, not patched.
+- Goldens must be bit-identical in the container (platform-independent by design); a container hash difference is a real finding.
+- Build-artifact isolation: a second run on either platform must never be poisoned by the first (bin/, tools/raylib-sw/shadow, goldens/_reports/ never cross legs).
+- Env files read-only; nothing secret committed; app*.bin / exe outputs gitignored.
+
+**Ask First:** nothing — design decisions (base image, isolation mechanism, summary format) are delegated by the briefing ("your call" / "your design").
+
+**Never:** no GH workflow edits, no raylib/harness source changes to force the container green, no `--force` on the experimental windows gate, no committed binaries.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Full suite, container | `tools/ci-local.sh` (docker running) | build image (cached layers) → all 8 gates in container, per-gate ✅/❌ summary, exit 0 | any gate fails → stop, summary shows ❌ + skipped, exit 1 |
+| Fast loop | `--fast` | gates 1–2 only, container | same stop-on-fail |
+| Native mac | `--mac` | 8 gates natively; odin version mismatch → LOUD warning, proceed | odin missing → clear error |
+| Docker not running / absent | default mode | plain-language "Docker is not running" message | exit 1, no cryptic socket errors |
+| Container artifacts | run 1 then run 2 | both green; run 2 unaffected by run 1 (fresh container filesystem + gitignored exclusions) | n/a |
+| Windows cross | `--windows-cross` | attempt `-target:windows_amd64`; mac distro refuses ("Linking for cross compilation … not yet supported") | capture failure output, exit 0-with-warning, document in PR |
+| Goldens differ in container | harness run | REAL finding: report, do not paper over | exit 1 with report path (host `goldens/_reports/` bind-mount) |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
+
+## Code Map
+
+- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — THE spec (read-only): 8 gates + asset naming + apt deps
+- `tools/lint.sh` — gate 1 (greps; uses python3 for the ASCII scanner)
+- `tools/harness.sh` — gates 4/5/6/8 driver (auto-builds the rlsw shadow via `tools/build_raylib_sw.sh` when missing)
+- `tools/build_raylib_sw.sh` — rlsw shadow builder (clones raylib 6.0, compiles with `cc`+`ar`; `odin root` required)
+- `.odin-version` — the pin (`dev-2026-08`); release asset names confirmed: `odin-linux-{amd64,arm64}-dev-2026-08.tar.gz`
+- `README.md` — docs home (docs/ has no dev-docs home; only captures/ + routing-explorer.html)
+- `.gitignore` — `bin/`, `tools/raylib-sw`, `goldens/_reports/`, `app*.bin` already ignored; add the windows-cross output
+- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/spec-local-ci-suite.md` — this spec
+
+## Tasks & Acceptance
+
+**Execution:**
+- [x] `Dockerfile.ci` (repo root, NEW) — ubuntu 24.04 slim (matches ubuntu-latest); apt: build-essential, git, curl, ca-certificates, python3, libx11-dev libxcursor-dev libxrandr-dev libxinerama-dev libxi-dev libgl1-mesa-dev; arch-aware pinned-odin tarball install (TARGETARCH); bake the rlsw shadow (`tools/build_raylib_sw.sh`) so warm runs skip the 40s clone+compile; COPY the tree (`.dockerignore` excludes .git/_bmad/.agents/.lavish/bin/tools/raylib-sw/goldens/_reports/app*.bin/*.dSYM/.env/_bmad-output/**/.build); `chmod -R a+rwX /src` + WORKDIR /src so the container can run as the host uid.
+- [x] `tools/ci-local.sh` (NEW) — one entrypoint: `--in-container` internal mode runs the 8-gate list with per-gate ✅/❌ summary + GH-step mapping; default host mode = docker build (cached) + run with `--user $(id -u):$(id -g)` and `goldens/_reports` bind-mount (with a write pre-flight probe); `--fast` gates 1–2; `--mac`/`--native` native run with odin-pin warning (token-compare; same-month nightly = informational note); `--windows-cross` experimental gate with report-and-warn semantics (probes the local toolchain by default, per briefing AC3); docker-down detection with a plain message; conflicting flag pairs rejected with exit 2.
+- [x] `.dockerignore` (NEW) — artifact + junk exclusions listed above.
+- [x] `.gitignore` — add the windows-cross output name (`app-win.exe`).
+- [x] `README.md` — "Local CI suite" section: usage, gate-mapping table (all 11 workflow steps), artifact-isolation note, known traps (odin pin warning, arch note, docker down, goldens bit-identical, fast-is-warm-only, timeouts, windows-cross semantics).
+- [x] `_pr_body.md` (tracked orphan from story 5.2, referenced by nothing) — removed in this PR; the PR body is authored fresh via `--body-file`.
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given a working Docker + this Mac, when `tools/ci-local.sh` runs at the PR sha, then all 8 gates pass in the container with a per-gate summary and exit 0; a second consecutive run is also green (no artifact poisoning).
+- Given the same Mac, when `tools/ci-local.sh --fast` runs, then gates 1–2 pass and stop there.
+- Given the same Mac, when `tools/ci-local.sh --mac` runs, then all 8 gates pass natively (rlsw shadow builds on first run).
+- Given the mac toolchain, when `tools/ci-local.sh --windows-cross` runs, then it either builds or reports the failure output and exits 0-with-warning (documented in the PR).
+- Given the PR, when `git diff v2 -- .github/workflows/ci.yml` is checked, then zero diff (byte-identical).
+- Given the PR body, when inspected, then it carries: the gate-mapping table, the artifact-isolation design choice, first-run + warm-run timings, and the windows-cross result.
+
+## Design Notes
+
+- **Artifact isolation (the deliberate choice):** the container leg never sees the host tree — the image COPYs the repo at build time (`.dockerignore` strips every artifact dir), so all linux build products live in the container layer and die with `--rm`. The ONLY host-writable surface is the `goldens/_reports/` bind-mount (gitignored scratch; failure diff bundles surface to the developer). The native mac leg builds into the worktree normally (also gitignored). Cross-leg poisoning is impossible by construction — no shared artifact state.
+- **Warm-run speed:** layer order maximizes docker cache: apt deps → `.odin-version`+odin tarball → `tools/` + baked rlsw shadow → rest of the tree. A source-only change re-copies one fast layer; the 40s raylib clone+compile runs once per image build, not per run.
+- **Parity by construction:** the container and native legs execute the SAME gate list in the SAME script (`--in-container` vs native mode), so the two legs cannot drift from each other or from the workflow.
+- **Container user:** `--user $(id -u):$(id -g)` + image `chmod a+rwX` keeps bind-mounted report files host-owned (no root-owned debris).
+- **Windows cross:** probe on this mac fails instantly — Odin mac distro: "Linking for cross compilation for this platform is not yet supported (windows amd64)"; `vendor:raylib/windows/` ships no lib. The gate reports and warns. The container leg gets its own probe during implementation (linux odin may support it via bundled lld); outcome documented either way.
+
+## Verification
+
+**Commands (all green at the PR sha, measured on this Mac, Apple Silicon):**
+- `tools/ci-local.sh` -- 8/8 ✅ container (run 1: 1m06s gates after a ~45s cold image build; run 2 warm: 33s) — both runs green, host tree proven artifact-free (`bin/`, `tools/raylib-sw/` absent after two container runs)
+- `tools/ci-local.sh --fast` -- 2 gates, exit 0 (2.6s warm container)
+- `tools/ci-local.sh --mac` -- 8/8 ✅ native (run 1 incl. rlsw shadow build: 41s; warm: 31s)
+- `tools/ci-local.sh --windows-cross` -- documented finding: odin dev-2026-08 cannot cross-link from mac OR linux (stderr message + exit 0 + NO binary — the gate detects the missing artifact, per the probe), exit 0-with-warning; identical result for the container-leg probe
